# FOAM Expo conventions

## Future layout (scaffold only when explicitly approved)

```
mobile/driver/              # FOAM Driver — app.foam.driver
mobile/ops/                 # FOAM OPS — app.foam.ops
packages/foam-staff-core/   # shared pure business logic
```

## Stack

- React Native, Expo, TypeScript
- Expo Development Builds for day-to-day work
- EAS Build when explicitly required

Do **not** assume Expo Go is the production architecture.

## Conventions

- Consistent navigation architecture across Driver and OPS
- Environment-aware configuration
- Public/mobile config is **public** — treat it as such

## Never hardcode in mobile

- production secrets
- Firebase Admin credentials / service account keys
- private API keys / Stripe secret keys / other server secrets

Sensitive operations stay server-side via the **existing** backend / Cloud Functions where appropriate.

## One platform

- Do not create a second backend or second database for mobile
- Do not create a parallel Firebase project unless explicitly approved
